@@ -41,3 +45,36 @@ parameters before the action runs, which can reject perfectly valid raw text
 requests to the bot endpoint as `text/plain` before Rack's method-override
 middleware, so the body stays untouched and `request.raw_post` is stored
 verbatim.
+
+## Webhooks
+
+A bot may have an optional `webhook_url`. When a message mentions a bot in a
+room the bot belongs to, `Message` enqueues `Bot::WebhookJob` after the message
+commit, so the person posting never waits on the bot's server.
+
+The job POSTs JSON with `Content-Type: application/json` to the webhook URL:
+
+    {
+      "event": "mention",
+      "author": { "id": 7, "name": "Alice" },
+      "room": { "id": 5, "name": "Ops", "reply_to": "/rooms/5/<bot_code>/messages" },
+      "message": {
+        "id": 118,
+        "body": { "text": "restart the build please", "html": "<div>… full rich-text body …</div>" },
+        "link": "/rooms/5/@118"
+      }
+    }
+
+`message.body.text` is the message text with the bot's own @-mention removed;
+`html` is the full rendered rich-text body. `room.reply_to` is the bot's own
+posting endpoint for that room, so it can reply asynchronously by POSTing a raw
+message body there. `message.link` opens the room scrolled to the mentioning
+message.
+
+A synchronous reply is a `200` response with `Content-Type: text/plain` or
+`text/html`: the response body is posted into the room as the bot, going through
+the same broadcast and notification path as any other message. A `204` response
+(or any other status or content type) posts nothing.
+
+Blank webhook URLs are normalized to nil, so saving the bot form with an empty
+webhook URL removes the webhook.
